    "created_at": "2022-01-25T22:59:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-01-25T22:59:41Z",
    "body": "> something where the developers switches the `media=\"\"` attribute to something matching later and expects the styles to be applied instantly.\r\n\r\nSounds like the opposite of async CSS: we don't need the stylesheet immediately but we still want the rendering to be blocked for no good reason...\r\n\r\nAnyway, I'm raising this issue partially because I want to see if script-blocking and render-blocking should behave consistently. If a `style` element with a mismatching `media` is script-blocking but not render-blocking, something seems off.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
